THE CONFRONTATION — XANGE.LOG
Version 0.9 | 2026-11-25

INDOOR / EXTERIOR ACOUSTIC FILTER

Doors can optionally define an interior room by a shared room ID and inclusive XYZ bounds. All doors for one room must use the same ID, bounds, and low-pass cutoff. A door is associated with the room when its interior bounds touch one of its two interaction sides. Invalid IDs, bounds outside the map, inconsistent definitions, and cutoff values outside 10–22000 Hz are rejected while parsing the map.

The room filter is active only while the player is inside the room bounds and every door with that room ID is closed. Opening any associated door or leaving the bounds disables it. The filter applies a low-pass DSP effect to active and newly loaded non-stationary spatial effects outside the interior bounds, plus exterior ambient sources. Sounds positioned wholly inside the room remain unfiltered. Music is excluded. The configured cutoff is the low-pass frequency in Hz; lower values remove more high-frequency exterior detail. Filter state is refreshed during world updates and when a door changes state. Door open/close sounds remain audible, with no spoken status announcements.

Map door records may append these 8 fields after the existing 13-field door record:
room_id:room_min_x:room_max_x:room_min_y:room_max_y:room_min_z:room_max_z:low_pass_cutoff_hz

Leave room_id empty to define a door without room acoustics. Use one identical room definition on each door that bounds the same interior.
